---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About QuoteShield — Independent Insurance Intelligence & Rate Research"
  description="Discover QuoteShield's mission, our credentialed editorial review board (CPCU, CFP®, CLU), and our rigorous 5-step insurance rating methodology."
>
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="badge badge-trust">Our Mission & Standards</span>
      <h1>Empowering American Consumers With Transparent Insurance Intelligence</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">
        We dismantle the complexity of auto, home, health, and life insurance policies with verified state rate filings, non-commission reviews, and certified financial expertise.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container page-content">
    <section class="section">
      <div class="grid-2">
        <div>
          <h2>Who We Are</h2>
          <p>
            Founded in 2024, <strong>QuoteShield</strong> is an independent consumer research organization dedicated to bringing radical transparency to the United States insurance marketplace. With over 6,000 licensed insurance companies operating across 50 states, consumers routinely overpay by hundreds—sometimes thousands—of dollars each year simply due to informational opacity.
          </p>
          <p>
            Unlike traditional lead-generation mills that sell your phone number to dozens of telemarketers, QuoteShield was built on an editorial-first principle: <strong>give consumers actionable, data-backed benchmarks before they request a quote</strong>. We aggregate public rate filings from the National Association of Insurance Commissioners (NAIC), cross-reference customer satisfaction indices from J.D. Power, and analyze financial solvency ratings from AM Best to provide real, unvarnished insight.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-card-box">
          <div class="stat-card">
            <span class="stat-num">50+</span>
            <span class="stat-label">National Carriers Monitored</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-card">
            <span class="stat-num">120K+</span>
            <span class="stat-label">Public Rate Filings Analyzed</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-card">
            <span class="stat-num">100%</span>
            <span class="stat-label">Independent Editorial Independence</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-card">
            <span class="stat-num">0</span>
            <span class="stat-label">Robocalls Sold</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Editorial Board -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2>Our Credentialed Editorial & Review Board</h2>
        <p>Every guide, calculator algorithm, and rate analysis is reviewed by licensed professionals holding premier insurance and financial designations.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="board-grid">
        <div class="board-member card">
          <div class="member-header">
            <div class="member-avatar">MV</div>
            <div>
              <h3>Marcus Vance, CPCU</h3>
              <span class="member-role">Senior Property & Casualty Analyst</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="member-bio">
            Marcus holds the prestigious Chartered Property Casualty Underwriter (CPCU) designation with over 18 years in commercial underwriting, state filing analysis, and auto risk modeling. He formerly advised state regulatory advisory committees and oversees QuoteShield's rate evaluation models.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="board-member card">
          <div class="member-header">
            <div class="member-avatar">ER</div>
            <div>
              <h3>Elena Rostova, CFP®</h3>
              <span class="member-role">Life & Retirement Planning Specialist</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="member-bio">
            Elena is a Certified Financial Planner™ professional specializing in personal risk mitigation, term vs. whole life policy structures, and estate liquidity. Her work has appeared across major national financial journals, helping families avoid predatory policy riders.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="board-member card">
          <div class="member-header">
            <div class="member-avatar">DS</div>
            <div>
              <h3>David Sterling, CLU</h3>
              <span class="member-role">Health & Medicare Policy Director</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="member-bio">
            David has spent 15 years dissecting Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (CMS) regulations, Medicare Advantage Star ratings, and ACA exchange plan designs. He ensures all QuoteShield health guidance aligns with current federal statutory frameworks.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- How We Rate Carriers -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Our 5-Pillar Carrier Evaluation Methodology</h2>
      <p>
        We evaluate every insurer across five weighted pillars to produce an objective, balanced score out of 5.0 stars:
      </p>

      <div class="methodology-grid">
        <div class="method-card">
          <div class="method-num">01</div>
          <h4>Financial Solvency (25%)</h4>
          <p>We review AM Best, Fitch, and Standard & Poor’s financial strength ratings to guarantee the insurer can honor claims during catastrophic events.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="method-card">
          <div class="method-num">02</div>
          <h4>Claim Satisfaction (25%)</h4>
          <p>We analyze the NAIC National Complaint Index (measuring complaints per premium volume) and J.D. Power annual auto and property claims satisfaction studies.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="method-card">
          <div class="method-num">03</div>
          <h4>Coverage Breadth (20%)</h4>
          <p>We reward carriers that offer robust endorsements—such as OEM parts, accident forgiveness, water backup, and umbrella extensions—without exorbitant markups.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="method-card">
          <div class="method-num">04</div>
          <h4>Pricing Competitiveness (20%)</h4>
          <p>We analyze thousands of ZIP code rate filings for clean drivers, high-risk motorists, homeowners with varied credit scores, and different family sizes.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="method-card">
          <div class="method-num">05</div>
          <h4>Digital & App Usability (10%)</h4>
          <p>We audit mobile apps, digital claim submission speeds, self-service policy adjustment tools, and 24/7 customer support responsiveness.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Editorial Independence -->
    <section class="section callout">
      <div class="callout-title">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="currentColor"><path d="M12 2C6.48 2 2 6.48 2 12s4.48 10 10 10 10-4.48 10-10S17.52 2 12 2zm1 15h-2v-6h2v6zm0-8h-2V7h2v2z"/></svg>
        Our Editorial Independence Guarantee
      </div>
      <p class="callout-text">
        QuoteShield does not accept payment from insurers to alter carrier ratings, inflate scores, or remove critical editorial findings. While we may receive compensation when consumers click through our links to request quotes or purchase policies, our editorial review team operates independently of commercial partnerships. Our reviews reflect authentic data, regulatory filings, and certified professional scrutiny.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0c1e33 0%, #153252 100%);
    color: #ffffff;
    padding: 3.5rem 0 3rem;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .page-header h1 {
    color: #ffffff;
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    margin: 1rem 0 0.75rem;
    max-width: 850px;
  }

  .subtitle {
    color: #cbd5e1;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    max-width: 750px;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .page-content {
    max-width: 1000px;
  }

  .section {
    margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
  }

  .section-heading {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .grid-2 {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  @media (min-width: 820px) {
    .grid-2 {
      grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 0.8fr;
    }
  }

  .stat-card-box {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .stat-card {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    text-align: center;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
  }

  .stat-num {
    display: block;
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .stat-label {
    font-size: 0.825rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .board-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .board-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .board-member {
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .member-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .member-avatar {
    width: 48px;
    height: 48px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-primary);
    color: #ffffff;
    font-weight: 700;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .member-header h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.15rem;
  }

  .member-role {
    font-size: 0.775rem;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-weight: 600;
    display: block;
  }

  .member-bio {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .methodology-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .methodology-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .method-card {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .method-num {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: #e2e8f0;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .method-card h4 {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .method-card p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
